IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld) -- THE TIME RULES, in one self-contained module.
--
-- This module imports only `prelude` and `daydate`, and no other module of this encoding, so it can be
-- copied unchanged, by itself, into other work.  Its own tests are in qld-tests-time.l4.
-- Every function carries an @ref to the section (or Schedule 1 definition) it implements, and its name says
-- what it computes and which provision it implements.
--
-- Counting follows the text.  A day is a calendar date.  The Act does not define "day" or "week";
-- a period of weeks returns NOTHING (not covered).  `Date day month year` rolls an impossible date forward,
-- so the month rule of Schedule 1 ("calendar month") is written out here and does not use `add months`.
--
-- Facts the Act leaves to other instruments are inputs: the holidays of a place (Schedule 1, "public holiday",
-- "business day"), the days an office is closed (s 38(5)(a)), and the time at which a letter would be
-- delivered in the ordinary course of post (s 39A(1)(b)).

§ `Reckoning time under the Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld)`

§§ `Moments within a day`

-- A moment is a calendar day and a number of seconds after the beginning of that day.
-- The end of a day is 86400 seconds after its beginning, which is the same instant as the beginning of the next day.
DECLARE `Moment in a day` HAS
    `the calendar day` IS A DATE
    `seconds after the beginning of that calendar day` IS A NUMBER

`the number of seconds in a day` MEANS 86400

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Moment in a day`
DECIDE `the beginning of a day` IS
    `Moment in a day` WITH
        `the calendar day` IS `the day`
        `seconds after the beginning of that calendar day` IS 0

-- Schedule 1, "midnight": "in relation to a particular day, means the point of time at which the day ends".
-- src:1335 | midnight, in relation to a particular day, means the point of time at which the day ends.
@ref Schedule 1 definition midnight (src:1335-1335)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Moment in a day`
DECIDE `midnight of a day, the point of time at which the day ends (Schedule 1)` IS
    `Moment in a day` WITH
        `the calendar day` IS `the day`
        `seconds after the beginning of that calendar day` IS `the number of seconds in a day`

GIVEN moment IS A `Moment in a day`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the instant of a moment` IS
    (Day (moment's `the calendar day`) TIMES `the number of seconds in a day`)
        PLUS moment's `seconds after the beginning of that calendar day`

GIVEN first IS A `Moment in a day`
      second IS A `Moment in a day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first moment is the same instant as the second moment` IF
    `the instant of a moment` first EQUALS `the instant of a moment` second

GIVEN first IS A `Moment in a day`
      second IS A `Moment in a day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first moment is before the second moment` IF
    `the instant of a moment` first LESS THAN `the instant of a moment` second

-- `the day after` and `the day before` are daydate's own (DATE to DATE).

§§ `Commencement, expiry and automatic repeal (Parts 5 and 6)`

-- src:202 | 15A Commencement of Acts on date of assent
-- src:203 | An Act commences on the date of assent except so far as the Act otherwise expressly provides.
@ref s 15A (src:202-203)
GIVEN `the date of assent` IS A DATE
      `the Act otherwise expressly provides for its commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the day an Act commences on the date of assent (s 15A)` IS
    IF `the Act otherwise expressly provides for its commencement`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the date of assent`

-- src:204 | 15B Time of commencement of Acts
-- src:205 | If an Act or a provision of an Act commences on a day, it commences at the beginning of the day.
@ref s 15B (src:204-205)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Moment in a day`
DECIDE `the moment a provision commences on a day (s 15B)` IS
    `the beginning of a day` `the day`

-- src:207 | (1) The provisions of an Act providing for its citation and commencement commence on the date of assent by force of this subsection.
@ref s 15C(1) (src:207-207)
GIVEN `the date of assent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Moment in a day`
DECIDE `the moment the citation and commencement provisions of an Act commence (s 15C(1))` IS
    `the moment a provision commences on a day (s 15B)` `the date of assent`

-- src:214 | 15D Commencement by proclamation etc.
-- src:215 | (1) If an Act or provisions of an Act is or are expressed to commence on a day to be fixed by proclamation or other instrument—
-- src:216 | (a) a single day or time may be fixed; or
-- src:217 | (b) different days or times may be fixed for different provisions.
-- src:218 | (2) If the day or time fixed by a proclamation for the commencement of an Act or a provision of an Act happens before the day on which the proclamation is notified (the notification day)—
-- src:219 | (a) the proclamation is valid; but
-- src:220 | (b) the Act or provision commences on the notification day.
@ref s 15D (src:214-220)
GIVEN `the day fixed by the proclamation` IS A DATE
      `the notification day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day an Act commences when a day is fixed by proclamation (s 15D)` IS
    IF `the day fixed by the proclamation` LESS THAN `the notification day`
    THEN `the notification day`
    ELSE `the day fixed by the proclamation`

-- src:283 | 18 Time of expiry of Act etc.
-- src:284 | If an Act or a provision of an Act—
-- src:285 | (a) expires on a day; or
-- src:286 | (b) is expressed to remain or continue in force, or otherwise have effect, until a day;
-- src:287 | the Act or provision has effect until the end of the day.
@ref s 18 (src:283-287)
GIVEN `the day the Act or provision expires or remains in force until` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Moment in a day`
DECIDE `the last moment an Act or provision has effect (s 18)` IS
    `midnight of a day, the point of time at which the day ends (Schedule 1)` `the day the Act or provision expires or remains in force until`

-- s 22C(1): an amending Act enacted after 30 June 1994 is automatically repealed at the beginning of the day after
-- all of its provisions have commenced.  "Enacted" is the fact of royal assent (s 15), so the date of assent is used.
-- src:381 | (1) An amending Act enacted after 30 June 1994 is automatically repealed at the beginning of the day after all of its provisions have commenced.
@ref s 22C(1) (src:381-381)
GIVEN `the date of assent` IS A DATE
      `the Act is an amending Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the last of its provisions commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE OF `Moment in a day`
DECIDE `the moment an amending Act is automatically repealed (s 22C(1))` IS
    IF     `the Act is an amending Act`
       AND `the date of assent` GREATER THAN Date 30 6 1994
    THEN JUST (`the beginning of a day` (`the day after` `the day on which the last of its provisions commenced`))
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Postponed laws (s 15DA)`

-- s 15DA(2) and (3): a postponed law that has not commenced within 1 year of the assent day automatically commences
-- on the next day; a regulation made within that year may extend the period to not more than 2 years of the assent day.
-- The year is counted by s 38(1) and the Schedule 1 definition of calendar month (see "Periods" below).
-- src:221 | 15DA Automatic commencement of postponed law
-- src:222 | (1) In this section—
-- src:223 | assent day means the date of assent of—
-- src:224 | (a) if the postponed law is an Act—the Act; or
-- src:225 | (b) if the postponed law is a provision of an Act—the Act that enacts the provision.
-- src:226 | postponed law means an Act or provision of an Act that does not commence on the assent day because a provision of an Act postpones its commencement until a day fixed under an instrument.
-- src:227 | (2) If a postponed law has not commenced within 1 year of the assent day, it automatically commences on the next day.
-- src:228 | (3) However, within 1 year of the assent day, a regulation may extend the period before commencement under subsection (2) to not more than 2 years of the assent day.
-- src:229 | (4) The regulation mentioned in subsection (3) may be made under—
-- src:230 | (a) the Act that is the postponed law; or
-- src:231 | (b) the Act of which the postponed law is a provision; or
-- src:232 | (c) an Act that the postponed law amends;
-- src:233 | as if the Act mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) included a provision that had commenced and authorised the regulation to be made.
-- src:234 | (5) This section—
-- src:235 | (a) only applies to a postponed law enacted after 31 December 1994; and
-- src:236 | (b) applies to a postponed law unless an Act expressly states it does not apply.
-- src:237 | Example—
-- src:238 | The Hypothetical Act 1995 was assented to on 5 April 1995 and was expressed to commence on a day to be fixed by proclamation. If the Act was not commenced by 5 April 1996, it would commence on 6 April 1996 under subsection (2) unless a regulation had been made under subsection (3) extending time for commencement.
@ref s 15DA (src:221-238)
GIVEN `the assent day` IS A DATE
      `an Act expressly states that s 15DA does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months from the assent day to which a regulation has extended the period, or 0 if none` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)` IS
    IF     `the assent day` GREATER THAN Date 31 12 1994
       AND (NOT `an Act expressly states that s 15DA does not apply`)
       AND (   extension EQUALS 0
            OR (extension AT LEAST 13 AND extension AT MOST 24))
    THEN JUST (`the day after` (`the last day of calendar months in succession` months (`the day after` `the assent day`)))
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        extension MEANS `the months from the assent day to which a regulation has extended the period, or 0 if none`
        months MEANS IF extension EQUALS 0 THEN 12 ELSE extension

§§ `Periods: calendar months, years and days (s 38(1) and Schedule 1)`

-- Schedule 1, "calendar month": a period starting at the beginning of any day of 1 of the 12 named months and ending
-- (a) immediately before the beginning of the corresponding day of the next named month; or
-- (b) if there is no such corresponding day, at the end of the next named month.
-- The result is the last day of that month.
-- src:1131 | calendar month means a period starting at the beginning of any day of 1 of the 12 named months and ending—
-- src:1132 | (a) immediately before the beginning of the corresponding day of the next named month; or
-- src:1133 | (b) if there is no such corresponding day—at the end of the next named month.
@ref Schedule 1 definitions calendar month, named month (src:1131-1133)
GIVEN `the starting day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` IS
    IF `the starting day number` AT MOST `Days in month` `the next named month` `the year of the next named month`
    THEN `the day before` (Date `the starting day number` `the next named month` `the year of the next named month`)
    ELSE Date (`Days in month` `the next named month` `the year of the next named month`) `the next named month` `the year of the next named month`
    WHERE
        `the starting day number` MEANS DATE_DAY `the starting day`
        `the next named month` MEANS IF DATE_MONTH `the starting day` EQUALS 12 THEN 1 ELSE DATE_MONTH `the starting day` PLUS 1
        `the year of the next named month` MEANS IF DATE_MONTH `the starting day` EQUALS 12 THEN DATE_YEAR `the starting day` PLUS 1 ELSE DATE_YEAR `the starting day`

-- A period of several months is read as that many calendar months in succession: each starts at the beginning of the
-- day after the previous one ended.
-- src:1339 | month means a calendar month.
@ref Schedule 1 definition month (src:1339-1339)
GIVEN `the number of months` IS A NUMBER
      `the starting day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day of calendar months in succession` IS
    IF `the number of months` AT MOST 1
    THEN `the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` `the starting day`
    ELSE `the last day of calendar months in succession` (`the number of months` MINUS 1) (`the day after` (`the last day of the calendar month starting at the beginning of a day (Schedule 1)` `the starting day`))

-- Schedule 1, "calendar year": a period of 12 months beginning on 1 January; "year": without specifying the type of year, means calendar year.
-- src:1134 | calendar year means a period of 12 months beginning on 1 January.
@ref Schedule 1 definitions calendar year, year (src:1134-1134)
GIVEN `the year number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the first day of the calendar year (Schedule 1)` IS Date 1 1 `the year number`

-- src:1134 | calendar year means a period of 12 months beginning on 1 January.
@ref Schedule 1 definition calendar year (src:1134-1134)
GIVEN `the year number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day of the calendar year (Schedule 1)` IS
    `the last day of calendar months in succession` 12 (`the first day of the calendar year (Schedule 1)` `the year number`)

-- Schedule 1, "financial year": a period of 1 year beginning on 1 July.
-- src:1248 | financial year means a period of 1 year beginning on 1 July.
@ref Schedule 1 definition financial year (src:1248-1248)
GIVEN `the year number in which the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day of the financial year beginning on 1 July (Schedule 1)` IS
    `the last day of calendar months in succession` 12 (Date 1 7 `the year number in which the financial year begins`)

DECLARE `Unit of a period` IS ONE OF
    `a number of days`
    `a number of weeks`
    `a number of calendar months`
    `a number of years`

DECLARE `Length of a period` HAS
    `how many` IS A NUMBER
    `in what unit` IS A `Unit of a period`

-- s 38(1) excludes the given day, so a period of days "beginning on" a day D has D PLUS 1 as its first day and D PLUS n as its last.
-- A period of weeks is not covered: the Act does not define "week" or say how many days one has.
-- A period of years is read as 12 calendar months for each year (see the fork register in NOTES.md).
-- s 38(1) is read as applying to periods of every unit, so a period of months begins at the beginning of the day after the given day.
-- src:825 | (1) If a period beginning on a given day, act or event is provided or allowed for a purpose by an Act, the period is to be calculated by excluding the day, or the day of the act or event, and—
-- src:826 | (a) if the period is expressed to be a specified number of clear days or at least a specified number of days—by excluding the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled; and
-- src:827 | (b) in any other case—by including the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled.
@ref s 38(1) (src:825-827)
-- src:1131 | calendar month means a period starting at the beginning of any day of 1 of the 12 named months and ending—
-- src:1132 | (a) immediately before the beginning of the corresponding day of the next named month; or
-- src:1133 | (b) if there is no such corresponding day—at the end of the next named month.
-- src:1134 | calendar year means a period of 12 months beginning on 1 January.
@ref Schedule 1 definitions calendar month, calendar year, month, year (src:1131-1134)
GIVEN `the given day` IS A DATE
      `the length of the period` IS A `Length of a period`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` IS
    IF `the length of the period`'s `how many` LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the length of the period`'s `in what unit`
        WHEN `a number of days` THEN JUST (`the given day` PLUS `the length of the period`'s `how many`)
        WHEN `a number of weeks` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `a number of calendar months` THEN JUST (`the last day of calendar months in succession` (`the length of the period`'s `how many`) (`the day after` `the given day`))
        WHEN `a number of years` THEN JUST (`the last day of calendar months in succession` (12 TIMES `the length of the period`'s `how many`) (`the day after` `the given day`))

-- s 38(1)(a): for a specified number of clear days, or at least a specified number of days, the day on which the purpose is
-- to be fulfilled is excluded as well, so the earliest day on which the purpose can be fulfilled is the day after the last day counted.
-- src:826 | (a) if the period is expressed to be a specified number of clear days or at least a specified number of days—by excluding the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled; and
@ref s 38(1)(a) (src:826-826)
GIVEN `the given day` IS A DATE
      `the number of clear days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the earliest day on which the purpose can be fulfilled after clear days (s 38(1)(a))` IS
    IF `the number of clear days` LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the day after` (`the given day` PLUS `the number of clear days`))

-- s 38(1)(b): in any other case the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled is included, so it can be the last day counted.
-- src:827 | (b) in any other case—by including the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled.
@ref s 38(1)(b) (src:827-827)
GIVEN `the given day` IS A DATE
      `the number of days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the last day on which the purpose can be fulfilled within days (s 38(1)(b))` IS
    IF `the number of days` LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the given day` PLUS `the number of days`)

-- s 38(1): is a given day counted in a period that begins on it?  No: the day, or the day of the act or event, is excluded.
-- src:825 | (1) If a period beginning on a given day, act or event is provided or allowed for a purpose by an Act, the period is to be calculated by excluding the day, or the day of the act or event, and—
@ref s 38(1) (src:825-825)
GIVEN `the given day` IS A DATE
      `a day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a day is counted in a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` IF
    `a day of the period` GREATER THAN `the given day`

-- Whether the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled is counted: not for clear days or at least a number of days, yes otherwise.
DECLARE `Kind of period of days` IS ONE OF
    `a specified number of clear days or at least a specified number of days`
    `any other period`

-- src:826 | (a) if the period is expressed to be a specified number of clear days or at least a specified number of days—by excluding the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled; and
-- src:827 | (b) in any other case—by including the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled.
@ref s 38(1) (src:826-827)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of period of days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled is counted in the period (s 38(1)(a) and (b))` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a specified number of clear days or at least a specified number of days` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any other period` THEN TRUE

§§ `Days that are excluded days (s 38(2) to (5), Schedule 1)`

-- The place's holidays and the days an office is closed are facts for the person using the module; the Act does not list them.
DECLARE `Facts about the days of a place` HAS
    `the days on which the office is closed where the filing or registration must or may be done` IS A LIST OF DATE
    `the public holidays, special holidays and bank holidays in the place where the thing must or may be done` IS A LIST OF DATE

DECLARE `Purpose of the time` IS ONE OF
    `filing or registering a document`
    `anything other than filing or registering a document`

-- Schedule 1, "business day": a day that is not (a) a Saturday or Sunday; or (b) a public holiday, special holiday or bank holiday in the place.
-- src:1126 | business day means a day that is not—
-- src:1127 | (a) a Saturday or Sunday; or
-- src:1128 | (b) a public holiday, special holiday or bank holiday in the place in which any relevant act is to be or may be done.
@ref Schedule 1 definition business day (src:1126-1128)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      facts IS A `Facts about the days of a place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a business day (Schedule 1)` IF
        (NOT `is weekend` `the day`)
    AND (NOT elem `the day` (facts's `the public holidays, special holidays and bank holidays in the place where the thing must or may be done`))

-- s 38(5): an excluded day is, for filing or registering a document, a day on which the office is closed; otherwise a day that is not a business day.
-- src:831 | (5) In this section—
-- src:832 | excluded day—
-- src:833 | (a) for filing or registering a document—means a day on which the office is closed where the filing or registration must or may be done; or
-- src:834 | (b) otherwise—means a day that is not a business day in the place in which the thing must or may be done.
@ref s 38(5) (src:831-834)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      purpose IS A `Purpose of the time`
      facts IS A `Facts about the days of a place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an excluded day (s 38(5))` IF
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `filing or registering a document` THEN elem `the day` (facts's `the days on which the office is closed where the filing or registration must or may be done`)
    WHEN `anything other than filing or registering a document` THEN (NOT `is a business day (Schedule 1)` `the day` facts)

-- s 38(2): a time, or last day of a period, calculated forwards that falls on an excluded day is taken to fall on the next later day that is not an excluded day.
-- The text does not limit this to periods counted in days, so it is applied to a last day however the period was counted.
-- src:828 | (2) If the time, or last day of a period, calculated forwards that is provided or allowed by an Act for doing anything falls on an excluded day, the time, or last day, is taken to fall on the next day later that is not an excluded day.
@ref s 38(2) (src:828-828)
GIVEN `the time or last day calculated forwards` IS A DATE
      purpose IS A `Purpose of the time`
      facts IS A `Facts about the days of a place`
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day a time or last day calculated forwards is taken to fall on (s 38(2))` IS
    IF `is an excluded day (s 38(5))` `the time or last day calculated forwards` purpose facts
    THEN `the day a time or last day calculated forwards is taken to fall on (s 38(2))` (`the day after` `the time or last day calculated forwards`) purpose facts
    ELSE `the time or last day calculated forwards`

-- s 38(3): calculated backwards, the time or earliest day is taken to fall on the next earlier day that is not an excluded day.
-- src:829 | (3) If the time, or earliest day of a period, calculated backwards that is provided or allowed by an Act for doing anything falls on an excluded day, the time, or earliest day, is taken to fall on the next day earlier that is not an excluded day.
@ref s 38(3) (src:829-829)
GIVEN `the time or earliest day calculated backwards` IS A DATE
      purpose IS A `Purpose of the time`
      facts IS A `Facts about the days of a place`
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day a time or earliest day calculated backwards is taken to fall on (s 38(3))` IS
    IF `is an excluded day (s 38(5))` `the time or earliest day calculated backwards` purpose facts
    THEN `the day a time or earliest day calculated backwards is taken to fall on (s 38(3))` (`the day before` `the time or earliest day calculated backwards`) purpose facts
    ELSE `the time or earliest day calculated backwards`

-- s 38(1) and (3): a period calculated backwards from a given day also excludes that day; the earliest day is n days before it.
-- The text says how backwards periods are adjusted off excluded days (s 38(3)) but not how one is counted; the exclusion
-- of the given day is read as the same in both directions.
-- src:825 | (1) If a period beginning on a given day, act or event is provided or allowed for a purpose by an Act, the period is to be calculated by excluding the day, or the day of the act or event, and—
@ref s 38(1) (src:825-825)
-- src:829 | (3) If the time, or earliest day of a period, calculated backwards that is provided or allowed by an Act for doing anything falls on an excluded day, the time, or earliest day, is taken to fall on the next day earlier that is not an excluded day.
@ref s 38(3) (src:829-829)
GIVEN `the given day` IS A DATE
      `the number of days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the earliest day of a period of days calculated backwards from a given day (s 38(1) and (3))` IS
    IF `the number of days` LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (Date (Day `the given day` MINUS `the number of days`))

-- The two steps together: the last day of a period, then the move off an excluded day.
-- src:825 | (1) If a period beginning on a given day, act or event is provided or allowed for a purpose by an Act, the period is to be calculated by excluding the day, or the day of the act or event, and—
-- src:826 | (a) if the period is expressed to be a specified number of clear days or at least a specified number of days—by excluding the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled; and
-- src:827 | (b) in any other case—by including the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled.
@ref s 38(1) (src:825-827)
-- src:828 | (2) If the time, or last day of a period, calculated forwards that is provided or allowed by an Act for doing anything falls on an excluded day, the time, or last day, is taken to fall on the next day later that is not an excluded day.
@ref s 38(2) (src:828-828)
GIVEN `the given day` IS A DATE
      `the length of the period` IS A `Length of a period`
      purpose IS A `Purpose of the time`
      facts IS A `Facts about the days of a place`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))` IS
    CONSIDER `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` `the given day` `the length of the period`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN JUST (`the day a time or last day calculated forwards is taken to fall on (s 38(2))` lastDay purpose facts)

§§ `No time provided (s 38(4))`

DECLARE `When a thing is to be done` IS ONE OF
    `as soon as possible, and as often as the relevant occasion happens`

-- src:830 | (4) If no time is provided or allowed for doing anything, the thing is to be done as soon as possible, and as often as the relevant occasion happens.
@ref s 38(4) (src:830-830)
GIVEN `a time is provided or allowed for doing the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE OF `When a thing is to be done`
DECIDE `when a thing is to be done if no time is provided (s 38(4))` IS
    IF `a time is provided or allowed for doing the thing`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `as soon as possible, and as often as the relevant occasion happens`

§§ `Age (s 38A)`

-- s 38A: a person is an age in years at the beginning of the person's birthday for the age.
-- The Act does not say which day is the birthday in a year with no 29 February for a person born on 29 February.
-- For that person the result for 28 February of such a year is NOTHING: 28 February is the birthday on one reading and
-- not yet the birthday on the other.  From 1 March of that year the age is reached on either reading.
-- src:835 | 38A Age
-- src:836 | For the purposes of an Act, a person is an age in years at the beginning of the person’s birthday for the age.
@ref s 38A (src:835-836)
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` IS
    IF `the day` LESS THAN `the date of birth`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF     DATE_MONTH `the date of birth` EQUALS 2
            AND DATE_DAY `the date of birth` EQUALS 29
            AND (NOT `is leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the day`))
            AND DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2
            AND DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 28
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF (DATE_MONTH `the day` * 100 PLUS DATE_DAY `the day`) AT LEAST (DATE_MONTH `the date of birth` * 100 PLUS DATE_DAY `the date of birth`)
             THEN JUST (DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS DATE_YEAR `the date of birth`)
             ELSE JUST (DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS DATE_YEAR `the date of birth` MINUS 1)

§§ `Service by post (s 39A)`

-- s 39A(1)(b): service by post is taken to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the
-- ordinary course of post, unless the contrary is proved.  The Act does not say how long the ordinary course of post takes,
-- so that time is an input.  When the contrary is proved the Act gives no time.
-- src:849 | (1) If an Act requires or permits a document to be served by post, service—
-- src:850 | (a) may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting the document as a letter; and
-- src:851 | (b) is taken to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post, unless the contrary is proved.
@ref s 39A(1) (src:849-851)
GIVEN `the time the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A `Moment in a day`
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE OF `Moment in a day`
DECIDE `the time service by post is taken to have been effected (s 39A(1)(b))` IS
    IF `the contrary is proved`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the time the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`

§§ `Acting appointments (s 24B(5) and (6))`

-- s 24B(5): the term of an acting appointment made because of a vacancy may not be more than 1 year; the appointee may be reappointed, and the term of each reappointment may not be more than 1 year.
-- The latest day on which the term can end is the last day of a period of 1 year beginning on the first day of the term (s 38(1)).
-- src:441 | (5) If the appointee is acting in the office because of a vacancy in the office—
-- src:442 | (a) the term of the appointment may not be more than 1 year; and
-- src:443 | (b) the appointee may be reappointed to act in the office, but the term of each reappointment may not be more than 1 year.
@ref s 24B(5) (src:441-443)
GIVEN `the first day of the term` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the latest last day of the term of an acting appointment because of a vacancy (s 24B(5))` IS
    `the last day of calendar months in succession` 12 (`the day after` `the first day of the term`)

-- s 24B(6)(c): the appointee may continue to act until the end of a year from the day of the vacancy (whichever of (a), (b) and (c) happens first).
-- src:444 | (6) If the appointee is acting in the office otherwise than because of a vacancy in the office and the office becomes vacant, then, subject to subsection (2), the appointee may continue to act until—
-- src:445 | (a) the appointer otherwise directs; or
-- src:446 | (b) the vacancy ends; or
-- src:447 | (c) the end of a year from the day of the vacancy;
-- src:448 | whichever happens first.
@ref s 24B(6) (src:444-448)
GIVEN `the day of the vacancy` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day an appointee may continue to act at the end of a year from the day of the vacancy (s 24B(6)(c))` IS
    `the last day of calendar months in succession` 12 (`the day after` `the day of the vacancy`)
